{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_gcaxm5dqfj33y4mprbvbg42ptfjxpap5ypu2xyvcgv5punaj3g5q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass, and I found and fixed a real bug.\n\n## What the library is\n\nTwo exported C symbols: `driver(const char*)` (parses an int with `strtol`, then runs a \"house\" simulation twice, printing 4 lines per run) and `run(house_t*, int)` — the low-level entry point, exported but *not* in the public header.\n\n## Results against the completion gate\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo check` clean | PASS |\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` diff C → Rust | **empty**; `ldd -r` clean, 0 unresolved own-code symbols |\n| Phase B — all 30 `CONFIGS.md` rows | PASS |\n| Phase C — all 12 `ERRORS.md` rows | PASS |\n| Every feature combo | 1 combo (no `[features]`), PASS |\n\n53 tests, ~14 000 differential comparisons, run in **both** `dev` and `release` plus a hardened `-C debug-assertions=on -C overflow-checks=on` build. Every comparison loads both `.so`s via `libloading` and checks stdout byte-for-byte, `house_t` field-by-field with `bathrooms` compared by **raw IEEE-754 bits**.\n\n## Two significant bugs found\n\n**1. A real behavioural divergence (`ERRORS.md` E11).** `run(NULL, x)` gave `SIGABRT` in Rust but `SIGSEGV` in C. The translation did `&mut *the_house` and then `(*house).floors`; both make rustc emit a null-validity check that `abort()`s under debug assertions. **Release hid it entirely** — only testing the debug profile exposed it. Fixed by going through `&raw const`/`&raw mut` + `ptr::read`/`ptr::write`, which lower to the same plain load/store the C emits.\n\n**2. A harness bug that made the whole suite meaningless.** `cargo test` does **not** rebuild a `cdylib`-only library. My first suite was validating a *stale* `.so` — I deliberately broke the Rust and all 49 tests still passed. Fixed with `crate-type = [\"cdylib\", \"rlib\"]` plus a harness guard that picks the newest artifact and hard-fails on `STALE cdylib`.\n\nBecause of #2 I mutation-tested the suite: 15 injected faults, all caught (3–30 failing tests each). The one undetected mutation — deleting the `errno == 0` conjunct — is *provably* unobservable on LP64, since `strtol`'s only `ERANGE` returns (`LONG_MAX`/`LONG_MIN`) already fail the `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX` check. I kept the check in the Rust for structural fidelity and documented why.\n\n## C oddities replicated, not \"fixed\"\n- Trailing garbage accepted (`endp != str` is checked, `*endp == '\\0'` never is): `\"12abc\"`→12, `\"7.9\"`→7, `\"0x10\"`→0.\n- Signed overflow wraps (`wrapping_add`), matching the `-O0` C build.\n- GCC rewrites the error `printf` into `puts`; LLVM does the same, and the tests pin the output to exactly 18 bytes.\n\nArtifacts: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `VERIFICATION.md`, `run_tests.sh`, `check_features.sh`. Nothing in `c_src/` was modified (verified).\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: `--test-threads=1` is mandatory, since stdout capture is done at the file-descriptor level and is process-global. Both scripts set it, but a bare `cargo test` will produce spurious failures."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1133,"cache_read_input_tokens":129032,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1133,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4ec62f0-7373-486b-b5a3-0e94cb8c1afc","uuid":"453de24b-bc04-453d-b905-0e2a49ada795","timestamp":"2026-08-28T14:23:53.058Z"}
